\ Benchmark: the flagged half of the per-element quotation bracket pair.
\
\ The timed body is the quotation `#each` runs once per element. A quotation reached as a runtime
\ value compiles into a standalone function. That function opens its own transient lexical frame
\ when the may-define analysis flags it. `@get` can install a word through its module arm, so this
\ one is flagged. On a hash `@get` installs nothing, so what the flagged run pays over its twin is
\ the frame.
\
\ The bare twin is quotation_bracket_each_bare.1z. It differs in one word. Both natives pop the key
\ and the receiver, extract the key string, and read the same map. One pushes the value and the
\ other a boolean. So the lookup either side pays is the same.
\
\ The sequence is a string because an array literal is not a simple AOT literal. The loop is a
\ tail-recursive word for AOT compatibility.

test-str: ( -- s ) const [ "abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz" ] ;
test-hash: ( -- h ) const [ H{ k: 1 } ] ;

bench-each: ( n -- ) [
  dup 0 = [ drop ] [
    1 - test-str [ drop test-hash k: @get drop ] #each bench-each
  ] if
] ;

15000 bench-each

"done" print-line
